## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Email/Password Auth:** NextAuth supports email/password (Credentials provider), but it requires us to securely hash passwords (using bcrypt) and store them in the database manually. Do you want to build the Email/Password flow yourself, or should we make this portal **Google-only** for simplicity and security? (Google-only is highly recommended for college portals to ensure only verified students get in).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **NextAuth vs Auth.js v5:** NextAuth is currently transitioning to Auth.js v5 (which natively supports Next.js App Router and Server Actions). I recommend we use the `beta` version of Auth.js v5 for the most modern architecture. Does that sound good?

